  (2, 62, 63, $q$ध्यायतो विषयान् पुंसः सङ्गस्तेषूपजायते।
सङ्गात्सञ्जायते कामः कामात्क्रोधोऽभिजायते॥
क्रोधाद्भवति संमोहः संमोहात्स्मृतिविभ्रमः।
स्मृतिभ्रंशाद् बुद्धिनाशो बुद्धिनाशात्प्रणश्यति॥$q$, null, $q$Repeatedly thinking about an object creates attachment; attachment creates desire; frustrated desire creates anger. Anger leads to confusion, loss of memory and judgement, and eventually self-destruction.$q$, $q$The chain that leads to anger$q$, $q$Interrupt the chain early. Reduce obsessive scrolling, comparison, fantasy, and repeated attention to things that trigger unhealthy craving.$q$, '{equanimity,mind}'::text[]),
  (2, 64, 65, $q$रागद्वेषवियुक्तैस्तु विषयानिन्द्रियैश्चरन्।
आत्मवश्यैर्विधेयात्मा प्रसादमधिगच्छति॥
प्रसादे सर्वदुःखानां हानिरस्योपजायते।
प्रसन्नचेतसो ह्याशु बुद्धिः पर्यवतिष्ठते॥$q$, null, $q$One who moves through the world without being controlled by attraction and hatred gains inner serenity. From serenity comes clarity and relief from suffering.$q$, $q$Self-control produces clarity$q$, $q$The goal is not necessarily to avoid everything enjoyable. It is to enjoy without becoming dependent or enslaved.$q$, '{equanimity,mind}'::text[]),
  (2, 70, 71, $q$आपूर्यमाणमचलप्रतिष्ठं समुद्रमापः प्रविशन्ति यद्वत्।
