कौन्तेय प्रतिजानीहि न मे भक्तः प्रणश्यति॥$q$, null, $q$Even a person who has behaved very badly can become righteous through wholehearted transformation. Such a person should not be permanently defined by the past.$q$, $q$Transformation is possible$q$, $q$Allow people—including yourself—to change, while still expecting accountability and responsible action. Forgiveness does not require ignoring harm.$q$, '{faith,dharma}'::text[]),
  (10, 4, 5, $q$बुद्धिर्ज्ञानमसंमोहः क्षमा सत्यं दमः शमः।
सुखं दुःखं भवोऽभावो भयं चाभयमेव च॥
अहिंसा समता तुष्टिस्तपो दानं यशोऽयशः।
भवन्ति भावा भूतानां मत्त एव पृथग्विधाः॥$q$, null, $q$Intelligence, knowledge, clarity, forgiveness, truth, self-control, peace, happiness, sorrow, courage, fearlessness, nonviolence, equality, contentment, discipline, charity, fame, and dishonour are all qualities found in life.$q$, $q$Cultivate noble qualities$q$, $q$Recognise that people have different tendencies, but consciously cultivate the qualities that lead to wisdom and compassion.$q$, '{faith,dharma}'::text[]),
  (10, 10, null, $q$तेषां सततयुक्तानां भजतां प्रीतिपूर्वकम्।
ददामि बुद्धियोगं तं येन मामुपयान्ति ते॥$q$, null, $q$To those who remain devoted and sincerely connected, the Divine gives the wisdom by which they reach the highest truth.$q$, $q$Dedication brings clarity$q$, $q$Clarity often comes after consistent practice, sincere effort, and commitment—not before beginning.$q$, '{faith,dharma}'::text[]),
  (10, 20, null, $q$अहमात्मा गुडाकेश सर्वभूताशयस्थितः।
अहमादिश्च मध्यं च भूतानामन्त एव च॥$q$, null, $q$The Divine Self dwells in the heart of every being and is the beginning, middle, and end of all life.$q$, $q$The Divine presence within$q$, $q$Remember your deeper dignity and the dignity of others. Do not reduce yourself or anyone else to a job title, mistake, body, or social identity.$q$, '{faith,dharma}'::text[]),
  (12, 13, 14, $q$अद्वेष्टा सर्वभूतानां मैत्रः करुण एव च।
निर्ममो निरहङ्कारः समदुःखसुखः क्षमी॥
सन्तुष्टः सततं योगी यतात्मा दृढनिश्चयः।
मय्यर्पितमनोबुद्धिर्यो मद्भक्तः स मे प्रियः॥$q$, null, $q$A beloved devotee is free from hatred, friendly, compassionate, humble, balanced in pleasure and pain, forgiving, content, self-controlled, and firm in purpose.$q$, $q$The qualities of a good human being$q$, $q$Use this as a daily character checklist: Am I becoming kinder, less egoistic, more patient, and more emotionally balanced?$q$, '{self-mastery,mind}'::text[]),
  (12, 15, null, $q$यस्मान्नोद्विजते लोको लोकान्नोद्विजते च यः।
हर्षामर्षभयोद्वेगैर्मुक्तो यः स च मे प्रियः॥$q$, null, $q$The Divine loves the person who does not disturb others and is not constantly disturbed by others, and who is free from excessive excitement, anger, fear, and anxiety.$q$, $q$Do not disturb others unnecessarily$q$, $q$Before speaking, posting, or reacting, ask whether you are creating unnecessary disturbance.$q$, '{self-mastery,mind}'::text[]),
  (12, 17, null, $q$यो न हृष्यति न द्वेष्टि न शोचति न काङ्क्षति।
शुभाशुभपरित्यागी भक्तिमान्यः स मे प्रियः॥$q$, null, $q$A steady person is not excessively excited, hateful, sorrowful, or constantly longing, and does not become bound by attachment to favourable or unfavourable outcomes.$q$, $q$Freedom from emotional dependence$q$, $q$Do not allow praise, criticism, gain, loss, victory, or defeat to completely determine your emotional state.$q$, '{self-mastery,mind}'::text[]),
  (12, 18, 19, $q$समः शत्रौ च मित्रे च तथा मानापमानयोः।
शीतोष्णसुखदुःखेषु समः सङ्गविवर्जितः॥
तुल्यनिन्दास्तुतिर्मौनी सन्तुष्टो येन केनचित्।
अनिकेतः स्थिरमतिर्भक्तिमान्मे प्रियो नरः॥$q$, null, $q$A balanced person remains steady toward friend and enemy, honour and dishonour, pleasure and pain, praise and blame.$q$, $q$Equanimity in relationships$q$, $q$Listen to criticism without hatred and accept praise without becoming dependent on it.$q$, '{self-mastery,mind}'::text[]),
  (13, 8, 12, $q$अमानित्वमदम्भित्वमहिंसा क्षान्तिरार्जवम्।
आचार्योपासनं शौचं स्थैर्यमात्मविनिग्रहः॥
इन्द्रियार्थेषु वैराग्यमनहङ्कार एव च।
जन्ममृत्युजराव्याधिदुःखदोषानुदर्शनम्॥
असक्तिरनभिष्वङ्गः पुत्रदारगृहादिषु।
नित्यं च समचित्तत्वमिष्टानिष्टोपपत्तिषु॥
मयि चानन्ययोगेन भक्तिरव्यभिचारिणी।
विविक्तदेशसेवित्वमरतिर्जनसंसदि॥
अध्यात्मज्ञाननित्यत्वं तत्त्वज्ञानार्थदर्शनम्।
एतज्ज्ञानमिति प्रोक्तमज्ञानं यदतोऽन्यथा॥$q$, null, $q$Wisdom includes humility, absence of pretence, nonviolence, patience, straightforwardness, purity, steadiness, self-control, freedom from ego, awareness of mortality, non-possessiveness, mental balance, devotion, self-reflection, and the ability to spend time in quietness.$q$, $q$A practical list of wisdom$q$, $q$Non-attachment to family and possessions does not mean neglecting them. It means loving and caring without possessiveness, control, or fear.$q$, '{self-mastery,mind}'::text[]),
  (13, 28, null, $q$समं सर्वेषु भूतेषु तिष्ठन्तं परमेश्वरम्।
विनश्यत्स्वविनश्यन्तं यः पश्यति स पश्यति॥$q$, null, $q$One truly sees who perceives the same imperishable Divine presence in all beings, even though bodies are temporary.$q$, $q$See the same Divine presence in all$q$, $q$This vision encourages compassion, nonviolence, humility, and respect for every person.$q$, '{self-mastery,mind}'::text[]),
  (14, 17, null, $q$सत्त्वात्सञ्जायते ज्ञानं रजसो लोभ एव च।
प्रमादमोहौ तमसो भवतोऽज्ञानमेव च॥$q$, null, $q$Clarity and knowledge arise from sattva; greed from rajas; negligence, confusion, and ignorance from tamas.$q$, $q$Understand your mental state$q$, $q$Before blaming yourself, check your sleep, diet, environment, stress, and habits. Sometimes clarity requires changing your conditions.$q$, '{equanimity,mind}'::text[]),
  (16, 1, 3, $q$अभयं सत्त्वसंशुद्धिर्ज्ञानयोगव्यवस्थितिः।
दानं दमश्च यज्ञश्च स्वाध्यायस्तप आर्जवम्॥
अहिंसा सत्यमक्रोधस्त्यागः शान्तिरपैशुनम्।
दया भूतेष्वलोलुप्त्वं मार्दवं ह्रीरचापलम्॥
तेजः क्षमा धृतिः शौचमद्रोहो नातिमानिता।
भवन्ति सम्पदं दैवीमभिजातस्य भारत॥$q$, null, $q$Fearlessness, purity, knowledge, charity, self-control, study, discipline, straightforwardness, nonviolence, truth, freedom from anger, peace, compassion, non-greed, gentleness, modesty, patience, courage, cleanliness, absence of hatred, and humility are divine qualities.$q$, $q$Divine qualities$q$, $q$Use these verses as a personal character audit. Ask which quality you need to strengthen today.$q$, '{faith,dharma}'::text[]),
  (16, 21, null, $q$त्रिविधं नरकस्येदं द्वारं नाशनमात्मनः।
कामः क्रोधस्तथा लोभस्तस्मादेतत्त्रयं त्यजेत्॥$q$, null, $q$Desire, anger, and greed are three gates leading to self-destruction. Therefore, one should abandon them.$q$, $q$Avoid three destructive tendencies$q$, $q$Treat uncontrolled craving, rage, and greed as warning signs—not as personality traits to be celebrated.$q$, '{equanimity,mind}'::text[]),
  (17, 15, 16, $q$अनुद्वेगकरं वाक्यं सत्यं प्रियहितं च यत्।
स्वाध्यायाभ्यसनं चैव वाङ्मयं तप उच्यते॥
मनःप्रसादः सौम्यत्वं मौनमात्मविनिग्रहः।
भावसंशुद्धिरित्येतत्तपो मानसमुच्यते॥$q$, null, $q$Verbal discipline means speaking truthfully, pleasantly, beneficially, and without causing unnecessary distress. Mental discipline means serenity, gentleness, self-control, and purity of intention.$q$, $q$Discipline of speech and mind$q$, $q$Before speaking, ask: Is it true? Is it useful? Is it kind? Is this the right time?$q$, '{self-mastery,mind}'::text[]),
  (18, 5, 6, $q$यज्ञदानतपःकर्म न त्याज्यं कार्यमेव तत्।
यज्ञो दानं तपश्चैव पावनानि मनीषिणाम्॥
एतान्यपि तु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा फलानि च।
कर्तव्यानीति मे पार्थ निश्चितं मतमुत्तमम्॥$q$, null, $q$Sacrifice, charity, discipline, and service should not be abandoned. They should be performed without attachment to personal rewards.$q$, $q$Do not abandon good actions$q$, $q$Continue helping, giving, studying, exercising, and serving even when nobody immediately notices.$q$, '{duty}'::text[]),
  (18, 26, null, $q$मुक्तसङ्गोऽनहंवादी धृत्युत्साहसमन्वितः।
सिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योर्निर्विकारः कर्ता सात्त्विक उच्यते॥$q$, null, $q$A noble worker is free from attachment, not egoistic, courageous, enthusiastic, steady, and undisturbed by success or failure.$q$, $q$The ideal attitude toward work$q$, $q$Be energetic without becoming arrogant, and ambitious without allowing achievement to define your entire identity.$q$, '{faith,dharma}'::text[]),
  (18, 30, null, $q$प्रवृत्तिं च निवृत्तिं च कार्याकार्ये भयाभये।
बन्धं मोक्षं च या वेत्ति बुद्धिः सा पार्थ सात्त्विकी॥$q$, null, $q$A clear intellect understands what should be done and avoided, what is fearful and fearless, and what leads to bondage or freedom.$q$, $q$Use discrimination before making decisions$q$, $q$Before making an important choice, ask: What are the long-term consequences? Will this increase freedom, wisdom, and responsibility—or dependence, fear, and regret?$q$, '{faith,dharma}'::text[]),
  (18, 33, null, $q$धृत्या यया धारयते मनःप्राणेन्द्रियक्रियाः।
योगेनाव्यभिचारिण्या धृतिः सा पार्थ सात्त्विकी॥$q$, null, $q$Steady determination is the strength by which a person holds the mind, vital energy, senses, and actions firmly to a disciplined path.$q$, $q$Develop steady determination$q$, $q$Motivation changes daily; disciplined commitment keeps you moving when motivation disappears.$q$, '{faith,dharma}'::text[]),
  (18, 45, 46, $q$स्वे स्वे कर्मण्यभिरतः संसिद्धिं लभते नरः।
स्वकर्मनिरतः सिद्धिं यथा विन्दति तच्छृणु॥
यतः प्रवृत्तिर्भूतानां येन सर्वमिदं ततम्।
स्वकर्मणा तमभ्यर्च्य सिद्धिं विन्दति मानवः॥$q$, null, $q$A person can attain fulfilment by sincerely performing their own work and dedicating it to the source of all life.$q$, $q$Make your work meaningful$q$, $q$Even ordinary work can become meaningful when performed with care, responsibility, and service-mindedness.$q$, '{duty}'::text[]),
  (18, 63, null, $q$इति ते ज्ञानमाख्यातं गुह्याद्गुह्यतरं मया।
विमृश्यैतदशेषेण यथेच्छसि तथा कुरु॥$q$, null, $q$I have explained this profound knowledge to you. Reflect on it fully, and then act according to your understanding.$q$, $q$Think deeply and choose responsibly$q$, $q$The Gītā encourages reflection, not blind obedience. Take advice seriously, think carefully, and accept responsibility for your decision.$q$, '{faith,dharma}'::text[]),
  (18, 66, null, $q$सर्वधर्मान्परित्यज्य मामेकं शरणं व्रज।
अहं त्वां सर्वपापेभ्यो मोक्षयिष्यामि मा शुचः॥$q$, null, $q$Take refuge in the Divine alone; I will free you from all wrongdoing—do not grieve.$q$, $q$Surrender fear and ego$q$, $q$This does not mean abandoning moral duties or responsibilities. It means surrendering ego, fear, guilt, and confusion to a higher truth while continuing to act rightly.$q$, '{faith,dharma}'::text[]),
  (18, 78, null, $q$यत्र योगेश्वरः कृष्णो यत्र पार्थो धनुर्धरः।
